# Read project context first

This repository keeps a running summary of decisions, architecture, and
conventions in `CONTEXT.md` at the workspace root. Before answering any
non-trivial question or making any changes, read that file using the Read
tool — it explains:

- What the project is (a Tauri v2 + React anime video player on Windows).
- The frontend / backend architecture and how they communicate.
- The critical mpv hosting decision (owned `WS_POPUP` top-level window
  instead of `WS_CHILD`, because of WebView2 + DirectComposition). Do not
  re-derive this; the trade-offs are documented.
- File layout, build commands, and conventions (PowerShell shell, comment
  style, no unprompted commits, run `cargo check` / `npx tsc --noEmit`
  after edits).

Also skim `TODO.md` so you know what follow-ups are already tracked
before proposing new ones.

If you change anything that contradicts or extends what's in `CONTEXT.md`
(architecture shifts, new conventions, new top-level files), update
`CONTEXT.md` in the same change so it stays accurate.
